# Line endings for sources and build files.
#
# Most of these files are stored with CRLF in the repository today. "text=auto"
# leaves a file whose committed version already contains CRLF exactly as it is
# (plain "text" would rewrite it to LF on its next commit), and "eol=crlf"
# checks every matching file out with CRLF, which matches the current
# convention. A one-time LF renormalisation is a separate decision.
*.c             text=auto eol=crlf
*.h             text=auto eol=crlf
Kconfig*        text=auto eol=crlf
CMakeLists.txt  text=auto eol=crlf
*.defaults      text=auto eol=crlf
